WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.350
Speaker 1: OK, we have lots of news to start
with today.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:07.290
Some good, some not so good and some absolutely
terrible.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.660
And we're starting there.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:14.340
What is taking place right now in the country
of India is almost beyond words.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:23.440
It's a complete humanitarian crisis as hospitals
are collapsing under the pressure of a covid

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.440
explosion.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:29.490
If you look at the numbers, I looked this
morning and thought there must be a mistake.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:33.620
It looks like they are almost literally off
the charts.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:39.100
And in fact, these numbers I'm going to show
you were probably underreported due to the

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.330
poor infrastructure in much of India.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.940
That is leading to people just dying in the
streets.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:51.559
That's not a figure of speech and potentially
not even being counted in the number of dead

00:00:51.559 --> 00:00:52.559
from covid.

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:58.680
So cases in India have surged to a pandemic
high of three hundred and twenty thousand

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.510
cases per day.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:03.649
India previously had just one peak in mid-September.

00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:06.320
They did a good job for a long time.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:11.799
This new peak is more than three times worse,
their previous peak and the deaths are just

00:01:11.799 --> 00:01:17.590
as bad, spiking most recently to about 2000
deaths per day.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:25.899
And again, probably under reports of the real
numbers because of the disconnected and rural

00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:31.320
nature of much of India, where we just don't
even know if these numbers are actually the

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.389
full story.

00:01:32.389 --> 00:01:37.600
Now, I think it's important to understand
as we sit in the United States and look at

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:42.889
this, that because of India's high population,
India has one point three, almost one point

00:01:42.889 --> 00:01:44.909
four billion people.

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:48.700
We have about 330 million here in the U.S.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:54.049
We still have higher per capita case rates
and per capita death rates than India from

00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:56.459
the start of the pandemic.

00:01:56.459 --> 00:02:02.560
The difference, of course, is that we never
saw rates of growth like this.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:08.209
If this continues for even two more weeks,
we could have a dramatically different story.

00:02:08.209 --> 00:02:13.170
And the level of hospital collapse that India
is experiencing is different than what happened

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.170
in the United States.

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:18.530
We did get to full ICU use and we had a very
brief period where we were getting to the

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.540
limit on ventilators.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:27.240
But what's happening with medical facilities
and supplies in India is tragically almost

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.360
unbelievable.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:31.150
They are out of ICU beds in many places.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.859
They are out of oxygen in many parts of the
country.

00:02:33.859 --> 00:02:40.769
I saw one report last night where they were
reporting from the main sort of meter for

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:42.329
the hospital's oxygen supply.

00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:49.609
It was just at zero people being left outside
of hospitals waiting for care.

00:02:49.609 --> 00:02:51.790
Some are just dying in the streets.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:54.569
The images are absolutely horrifying.

00:02:54.569 --> 00:02:59.950
New Delhi in particular, which doesn't produce
its own oxygen and is dependent on getting

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:05.599
help from other areas, it seems to call it
critical shape doesn't even really explain

00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:07.079
what it is that's going on there.

00:03:07.079 --> 00:03:13.090
A bunch of Delhi hospitals tweeted essentially
S.O.S. messages over the weekend saying we

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.090
need oxygen supplies.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:21.750
At least 20 critically ill people died on
Saturday after oxygen supply was delayed.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:26.480
They ran out and it took a period of time
before they were ever able to get more.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:31.860
Other countries are trying to help, but it
feels like it's started too late not to be

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:33.329
critical of people that are helping.

00:03:33.329 --> 00:03:40.060
But we saw this coming and we fortunately
now see Joe Biden sending ventilators and

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:42.349
PPE and test kits and more medications.

00:03:42.349 --> 00:03:43.640
Many other countries are doing the same.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.060
The UK is sending ventilators.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:50.499
Many countries are doing things, but arguably
too late to help many of the people that are

00:03:50.499 --> 00:03:53.209
dying daily at this point in time.

00:03:53.209 --> 00:03:57.739
And yes, there's also some vaccination happening
there relatively slowly.

00:03:57.739 --> 00:03:59.459
Some countries are sending more vaccines.

00:03:59.459 --> 00:04:03.069
We know from looking at the numbers here in
the US, it takes a while for the vaccines

00:04:03.069 --> 00:04:04.069
to make a difference.

00:04:04.069 --> 00:04:06.799
You start vaccinating after two weeks.

00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:13.060
That first dose provides 85 or 80 percent
protection that you need excuse me, that second

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:17.220
dose, and that is a slow process before it
makes an impact.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:22.720
Vaccination won't solve the current problem
happening in hospitals as we speak, with three

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.410
people dying every two minutes.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:31.490
Also going in very much the wrong direction
in terms of larger countries are to some degree

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:38.930
not like India, but the Netherlands, Germany
and Colombia are also seeing some modest upticks

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:40.750
in terms of larger countries.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:48.470
And by the way, my birth country of Argentina,
just a continued disaster there with a completely

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:56.440
incompetent leadership, lack of transparency,
strict but unenforced rules.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.070
Vaccine cronyism, one.

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:03.090
Elected official found with vaccines in his
trunk and said, oh, I was bringing them to

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:07.780
some hospital, I mean, just about everything
you can imagine, it's been happening in Argentina.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:13.930
I have friends who just flew down, vaccinated,
said that accurate mask wearing was at about

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.150
50 percent.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:20.780
Shop owners are all wearing masks from what
you read, but you walk in and the mask is

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:25.720
down over the throat like, you know, it's
a complete and total disaster.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.009
And the numbers there are also reflecting
that.

00:05:28.009 --> 00:05:33.830
So globally, you know, you actually need some
nuance to see what's going on.

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:39.180
You have some large countries like India that
are disproportionately making the global numbers

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:40.520
look bad.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:44.360
We see a resumed case decline in the United
States.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:53.460
We are now about three weeks from when Israel
saw cases go down 90 plus percent.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:57.909
It looks like we are going to start seeing
very good numbers last week I said we were

00:05:57.909 --> 00:05:58.909
four weeks away now.

00:05:58.909 --> 00:06:01.379
Now it looks like we are three weeks away.

00:06:01.379 --> 00:06:04.669
And then at the same time, if you look at
just the global picture, you say, are we really

00:06:04.669 --> 00:06:06.520
making any progress here?

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:10.490
We are, but we're also losing ground in certain
places.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:14.120
And it's going to be this will go into twenty,
twenty two.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:17.870
When you consider that many countries won't
even really be able to start vaccinating in

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:18.870
a serious way.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:23.270
Until then, never mind the issue of vaccinating
children, we hopefully are getting closer

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.949
to that.

00:06:24.949 --> 00:06:30.050
Submitted for approval on one vaccine for
Pfizer has submitted for approval on 12 to

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.050
15.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.470
They did that at the beginning of April.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:35.810
We should be days from the FDA reviewing that.

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:41.780
And hopefully we can expand that to 12 plus
so many different things to be looking at,

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:44.490
some good, some not so good.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.820
And what's going on in India.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.180
Absolutely terrible.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:53.789
Which makes this next story particularly difficult
to pass.

00:06:53.789 --> 00:07:00.900
The European Union will be opening to vaccinated
American travelers at some point this summer.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:08:00.509
Let's talk 

00:08:00.509 --> 00:08:42.560
about 

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:48.920
that next.

